From 8bb8f9ac6a9235fa15cd2f6e4c7f1c2371fc2de9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dan Peavey <sunmachine@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:03:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] volsmoke: tight bounds, adaptive step count, inside-smoke
 overlay

- Draw/march only the AABB of cells that currently hold density
  (recomputed in UpdateDensities), not the full grid extent. Render bounds
  follow it so leaf-system culling tightens too.
- Step count is now ray length inside the smoke / (cell * $stepscale),
  capped by $maxsteps: grazing rays take 2-3 steps, core rays take many.
  Replaces the fixed $steps.
- Feed the camera's trilinear local density into g_SmokeFogOverlayAlpha so
  the legacy fullscreen smoke overlay (and the HUD glow / place-name
  occlusion that already reads it) works for volumes. While the camera is
  in dense smoke the max step count drops to neo_volsmoke_inside_maxsteps.
- New convars: neo_volsmoke_maxsteps, _stepscale, _overlay, _overlay_dist,
  _inside_maxsteps.
